//! Std-only port of `scripts/gen_docs.py`: regenerate machine-owned
//! sections in the docs and run the stale-phrase scan.
//!
//! ```text
//! cargo run --release --example gen_docs -- [--root DIR]            # rewrite docs in place
//! cargo run --release --example gen_docs -- [--root DIR] --check    # exit 1 on drift / stale phrases
//! cargo run --release --example gen_docs -- --list-allow-stale | --check-tier-coverage | -h
//! ```
//!
//! `--root` (default: this crate's directory) is the checkout the script's
//! `REPO_ROOT` was; every other flag, message, generated byte and exit code
//! follows the Python script (CPython 3.12 semantics, see `pyport`). It reads
//! the same inputs: `coordinationhub/**/*.py` (module docstrings, LOC,
//! `TOOL_SCHEMAS`, `cli._COMMANDS`, `TOOL_DISPATCH`, `_CURRENT_SCHEMA_VERSION`,
//! `__version__`), `coverage.json`, and `python -m pytest --collect-only -q
//! tests/` for the test count.

